From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000249 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gemini Mainline Experiment <gemini-mainline@example.invalid>
Date: Mon, 10 Aug 2026 18:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] soc: mediatek: add cooperative MT6797 vendor owner adapter

Add a dormant vendor-aware owner adapter that composes the existing MT6797
identity, PPM, live-state, and calibrated-provider callback contracts. The
adapter validates each ABI, binds the callbacks to the resource owner, and
constructs the existing state-owner callbacks without registering them.

The adapter deliberately does not call the vendor PTP-table, voltage, or PPM
client registration setters: those are single callback slots and must be
chained by the vendor-aware driver integration itself. Hardware-free KUnit
coverage proves incomplete contracts are refused, complete contracts bind and
unbind, and lifecycle setup invokes no source callback.

This is an experiment-only contract and not submission-ready.
